<%- include('../partials/head') %>

<div class="pagehead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Shipping and transfers</h1>
    <p>How an item listed on this site physically reaches you.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <% if (transferConfirmed) { %>
      <h2>Firearm transfers</h2>
      <p><%= business.policy.transferProcessText %></p>
    <% } else { %>
      <div class="note note-pending">
        <h3>Transfer procedure pending</h3>
        <p>
          This section is deliberately blank. A firearm transfer procedure is a legal process specific to
          the dealer's licence and jurisdiction, and writing a plausible sounding version of it would be
          both wrong and dangerous. The licence holder supplies the exact wording, it is reviewed, and then
          it appears here.
        </p>
        <p>The wording needs to answer, at minimum:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Which licence or premises the firearm is shipped to, and whether a customer address is ever used.</li>
          <li>What identification and what background check the receiving party performs.</li>
          <li>Who pays the transfer fee and how much it is.</li>
          <li>How long the process normally takes.</li>
          <li>Which destinations are refused outright.</li>
          <li>What happens if the buyer fails the check after the item has shipped.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <h2>Parts and accessories</h2>
    <p>
      Slides, triggers and other parts are not always subject to the same transfer rules as a complete
      firearm, but some jurisdictions do regulate them. The shop confirms which route applies to your order
      when it replies to your request.
    </p>

    <h2>Costs</h2>
    <p>
      Shipping, transfer fees and tax are not calculated on this site. They depend on the destination, the
      receiving licence and the item, so a person quotes them on your order request rather than an estimate
      appearing at checkout. The price shown against a listing is the item price recorded in the stock
      system and nothing else.
    </p>

    <h2>Timescales</h2>
    <p class="meta-updated">
      Dispatch and delivery timescales are published here once the shop confirms them with its carriers. No
      timeframe is stated on this site until the shop can stand behind it.
    </p>

    <h2>Damage or a wrong item</h2>
    <p>
      Tell the shop within the window set out in the <a href="/returns-policy">returns policy</a>. Do not
      attempt to return a firearm by post without first agreeing the route with the shop, because unlawful
      shipping of a firearm is an offence in itself.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
